<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka Kelani up on growth prospects.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka Kelani up on growth prospects.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kelani Valley Plantations Ltd rose 16.67 percent or 3.75 rupees to 26.25 on good growth expected in 1997, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The plantation sector, which did very well in 1995 and 1996, is expected to perform well in 1997 due to good prices and demand for tea,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>Kelani Valley is one of six privatised plantation firms trading in Colombo</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (41) 434319</p>
</text>
